Mini Humanoid Power Distribution (25-DoF)

Goal: Provide regulated power to 25 Actuators (High-Voltage) and 1 Main Control Board (Low-Voltage) efficiently.

I. Power Source

Component

Specification

Function

Main Battery

3S LiPo (11.1V Nominal, 12.6V Max)

Primary power for the entire robot. Chosen for high energy density.

Voltage Range

9.0V (Min) - 12.6V (Max)

Defines the input range for all regulation stages.

II. Power Distribution Board (PDB) - Central Node

The PDB takes the main battery input and splits it into two primary rails:

A. High-Voltage (HV) Actuator Rail

Component

Specification

Function

Output Voltage

9.0V - 12.6V (Unregulated Battery Voltage)

This rail directly powers all 25 actuators. It avoids the inefficiency and heat of regulating a high-current load.

Protection

Polyswitch Fuses (e.g., 5A per limb bus)

Protects against short circuits in the servo lines.

Distribution

Connects to 5 separate Bus lines (Neck, R. Arm, L. Arm, R. Leg, L. Leg)

Simplifies wiring and localizes overcurrent issues.

B. Low-Voltage (LV) Logic Rail

Component

Specification

Function

Regulator

Buck Regulator (DC-DC Converter)

High efficiency for stepping down the battery voltage (12V) to 5V. Linear regulators would dissipate too much heat.

Output Voltage

5.0V (± 0.2V)

Standard operating voltage for the ESP12F microcontroller, sensors, and any low-power peripherals.

Output Current

~2A capacity (Must handle ESP + peripherals)

Ensures stable power for the control system during peak operation.

